+`POST /v1/coordinator/conversations/{id}/stop` durably stops the entire conversation:
+queued turns, dispatches, actions and result wakeups cannot start again. Results and
+receipts remain readable. The default `{}` stops exact goal runs and preserves shared
+workers. At conversation creation, `owned_worker_ids` can transfer fresh, unused,
+owner/project-scoped workers to that conversation. Existing workers cannot be claimed.
+A client requests `{"close_workers": true}` to close exclusively owned workers and
+their schedules, queued runs and follow-ups. The runtime requires its recorded claim,
+delegation or provider-session ownership and checks for other conversation references
+in the same transaction. Referenced/shared workers stay open; only this conversation's
+runs, turns, actions, wakeups and exact source-run schedules are cancelled. Owner-created
+schedules have no source run and remain active on shared workers. Native schedule creation
+records the authenticated source run, never a caller-supplied ownership assertion. That close intent
+commits with the conversation fence before runtime cancellation. The response remains
+`stopping` until every native turn releases capacity and every selected worker confirms
+termination, then returns `stopped`. Retry the same operation to recover after a failure;
+its worker scope cannot be downgraded. Single-goal Stop retains its existing run scope.
+
 Canonical generic instructions and tool descriptions live under
 `src/workers_projects_runtime/prompts/coordinator*`; `prompt_manifest()` exposes their hashes.
